  "Question": "Which of the following conditions establishes that \\(\\triangle ABC\\) is an isosceles triangle?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\angle A=30^\\circ\\), \\(\\angle B=50^\\circ\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\angle A=50^\\circ\\), \\(\\angle B=60^\\circ\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\angle A=20^\\circ\\), \\(\\angle B=60^\\circ\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\angle A=40^\\circ\\), \\(\\angle B=70^\\circ\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "In option D, \\(\\angle C=180^\\circ-40^\\circ-70^\\circ=70^\\circ=\\angle B\\), so the triangle is isosceles. In A, the angles are \\(30^\\circ,50^\\circ,100^\\circ\\); in B, \\(50^\\circ,60^\\circ,70^\\circ\\); and in C, \\(20^\\circ,60^\\circ,100^\\circ\\). Each of those triples has three unequal angles. Thus D is correct.",
